<title>UK: RESEARCH ALERT- Lehman cuts C&amp;W estimates.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT- Lehman cuts C&amp;W estimates.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Analysts at Lehman Brothers cut their earnings forecasts for Cable and Wireless Plc on Friday following the group's decision to raise its stake in Australian carrier Optus Communications.</p>
<p>C&amp;W shares were down 6-1/2p at 581-1/2p by 0839 GMT.</p>
<p>Lehman downgraded pre-tax profits to 1.401 billion stg from 1.463 billion for 1997/98 and to 1.662 billion from 1.712 billion for 1998/99.</p>
<p>However, it took the view that control of Optus came at a reasonable price, market sources said.</p>
<p>-- Elaine Hardcastle, London Newsroom +44 171 542 4027</p>
</text>
